### Business Processes – Two types of companies

**Administrative ERP** = core processes that ALL companies need:

| Process | What it does | Example |
|---|---|---|
| **Procure to Pay** | Buy things, pay suppliers | Buy laptops for employees |
| **Order to Cash** | Receive customer orders, deliver, get paid | Customer orders, you ship |
| **Record to Report** | Financial closing, reconciliations, taxes | Month-end closing |

**Operational ERP** = extra processes if you MANUFACTURE products:

| Process | What it does |
|---|---|
| **Idea to Market** | R&D designs the product, creates materials list |
| **Procure to Pay** | Buy materials you can't make yourself |
| **Plan to Fulfill** | Manufacture, quality check, store in warehouse |
| **Order to Cash** | Deliver to customer, handle returns |

**Two types of manufacturing:**
- 🧪 **Process manufacturing** – mix things that CANNOT be separated (e.g. pharmaceuticals, cake)
- 🔧 **Discrete manufacturing** – assemble parts that CAN be separated (e.g. car, phone)

